        """
    note """
        Windows Phase 8.5 now retains Sketch entropy deferral, ordered concurrent Full entropy candidates, and final-HF four-lane quantization at commit 2a788aed5969. The SIMD leaf is byte-identical and reduces the stable 4.3 MP thin median 5.08% (3.921 to 3.722 s); the 12 MP gain is 2.74%. Regenerated PGO gives a 3.501 s 4.3 MP median and the fresh matched-quality black-box gap is 8.59x cjxl; the fresh 12 MP ratio is 7.98x but thermally noisy. Windows stage diagnostics still point first to repeated Fast/navigation quantization, then Full entropy census/training and Count traversal. Linux perf/flamegraph attribution of at least 90% of samples remains required before selecting another leaf; keep the work active.
        """
    acceptance {
        check profile-justified {
            statement """
                Every leaf change targets at least 5% of current samples and improves end-to-end production-quality time.
                """
            method observation
        }
        check quality-preserved {
            statement """
                All decoder, target-rate, perceptual, and thread-determinism gates remain satisfied.
                """
            method command
