    note """
        Linux perf/flamegraph attribution is now complete at 98.3-98.9% symbolization with exact folded/event sums and zero lost samples. Retained coefficient-order caching removes an approximately 11% sort stack and improves paired thin t4 medians 18.14% at 4.3 MP and 23.64% at 12 MP; dense hybrid-token counts add 1.44% and 7.08% respectively. Retrained Linux PGO adds 12.28% on 4.3 MP and 12.42% on the unseen 12 MP input, without an LLVM profile warning. All Linux candidates are byte-identical to the immutable Linux baseline and the full workspace, target-rate, determinism, and oracle gates pass. Six of seven Windows anchors differ from Linux before/candidate-independently, so cross-platform byte identity needs separate diagnosis and is not used as this run's quality oracle. Post-PGO leaves are HF quantize_lane/traversal (about 10%/9%), pass-group writing (about 7%), census (about 6.6%), and entropy training (about 6-7%); keep the work active for those profile-qualified leaves.
        """
